<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Conflict resolution</span></p>
</td>
<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;" bis_size="{&quot;x&quot;:206,&quot;y&quot;:3071,&quot;w&quot;:410,&quot;h&quot;:85,&quot;abs_x&quot;:572,&quot;abs_y&quot;:4037}">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Two friends talk through a disagreement instead of avoiding each other</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 25pt;" bis_size="{&quot;x&quot;:22,&quot;y&quot;:3156,&quot;w&quot;:595,&quot;h&quot;:85,&quot;abs_x&quot;:388,&quot;abs_y&quot;:4122}">
<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;" bis_size="{&quot;x&quot;:22,&quot;y&quot;:3156,&quot;w&quot;:184,&quot;h&quot;:85,&quot;abs_x&quot;:388,&quot;abs_y&quot;:4122}">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Self-awareness</span></p>
</td>
<td style="vertical-align: top; padding: 5pt 5pt 5pt 5pt; overflow: hidden; overflow-wrap: break-word; border: solid #000000 0.5pt;" bis_size="{&quot;x&quot;:206,&quot;y&quot;:3156,&quot;w&quot;:410,&quot;h&quot;:85,&quot;abs_x&quot;:572,&quot;abs_y&quot;:4122}">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">A child recognises what makes them anxious and asks for help</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div style="margin-left: 0pt;" align="left">
<h2 style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Why does social emotional learning make academic learning possible?</span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Social emotional learning gives children the steadiness that academics depend on. A student who is anxious, disengaged or emotionally isolated struggles to concentrate, whatever the quality of teaching. Counselling builds that steadiness first, so classroom lessons reach a child who is ready to listen and take part, even when the work gets difficult.</span></p>
<ul style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; padding-inline-start: 48px;">
<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Anxiety uses up attention a child would otherwise spend on learning</span></p>
</li>
<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Feeling heard makes it easier to ask a teacher for help</span></p>
</li>
<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">A regulated child can persist through a hard chapter instead of giving up</span></p>
</li>
<li dir="ltr" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;" aria-level="1">
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Quality education, in the SDG sense, depends on these conditions being in place for every child</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">What Does A Real Counselling Look Like at DPS Kalyanpur?</span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Earlier this term, a Class 8 student was referred for being short-tempered and pulling away from her family, even though her friendships at school were strong. Follow-up sessions traced the change to shifting family attention and frequent comparisons with an older sibling. The counselling plan then addressed those causes directly.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">She had stopped sharing her thoughts and artwork with her parents.</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Her older sibling's exam preparation had drawn most of the family's attention.</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Comparisons at home were hurting her sense of self-worth</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Details are kept anonymous to protect the student</span></span></li>
</ul>
<div>
<h3 style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">What were the three shifts in the counselling plan?</span></h3>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">The plan asked the family to make three simple shifts at home, each aimed at a cause found in the follow-up sessions. One restored one-to-one attention, one ended the comparisons hurting her sense of self-worth and one turned her strongest interest into a channel for connection instead of a subject for judgement.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Fifteen minutes of daily exclusive time, with no talk about academics</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">A complete pause on comparison with her sibling</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Her love for art used as a bridge for connection instead of evaluation</span></span></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 16pt; margin-bottom: 4pt;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">What changed within four weeks?</span></h3>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Within four weeks, her parents reported fewer temper outbursts and she shared a drawing at home voluntarily for the first time in months. Better emotional regulation and more open family communication restored her sense of being valued, which underpins a child's willingness to engage with learning. Small changes at home made a large difference.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Fewer outbursts point to improved emotional regulation</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Sharing artwork again shows she felt safe with her family</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">The change came from small, consistent adjustments rather than a dramatic intervention</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">A child who feels valued has more energy left for the classroom</span></span></li>
</ul>
<div>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">How Do Parents and Teachers Work with the School Counsellor?</span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Parents and teachers are part of every plan. Teachers refer students and share classroom observations, parents report what changes at home and the counsellor combines both views into a support plan. This parent-teacher collaboration helps changes made in a session carry into daily routines, which is where they matter most.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Teachers notice mood and behaviour across a whole school day</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Parents see sleep, temper and communication at home</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">The counsellor turns both into small steps the family can follow</span></span></li>
<li><span><span style="background-color: transparent; font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #000000; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">Follow-up sessions check progress and adjust the plan</span></span></li>
</ul>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 18pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Why do SDG 3 and SDG 4 Go Hand in Hand in Schools?</span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">A school cannot deliver quality education to students who are anxious, disengaged or emotionally isolated. SDG 3 protects the child's well-being and SDG 4 depends on it. School wellness counselling that reaches every child equitably is where the two goals meet in an actual classroom. Neither can be met without the other.</span></p>
<div style="margin-left: 0pt;" align="left">
