<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">The smart choice? Find a balance. Pick a school that is accessible and academically strong. That&rsquo;s the sweet spot parents should aim for.</span></span></p>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Parent&ndash;School Partnership is a Must</span></span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Education works best when parents and schools work together. Look for schools that encourage communication. Regular parent-teacher meetings help. Progress updates keep parents informed. Feedback systems improve learning. When parents know what is happening in school, they can support their children better at home. And when both sides collaborate, students benefit the most.</span></span></p>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Safety and Security</span></span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 10pt; margin-bottom: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Secure transport is non-negotiable. Prioritise schools with 24/7 CCTV surveillance and trained security personnel. Also, a clean campus with hygienic facilities is a must. It helps parents stay worry free that their child learns and grows in an environment where safety is never an afterthought.</span></span></p>
<h2 dir="ltr" style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 14pt; margin-bottom: 6pt;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Lastly, Visit the Campus or Book a Virtual Tour</span></span></h2>
<p style="line-height: 1.7999999999999998; text-align: justify; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: #000000; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><span style="font-family: Georgia;">Online research helps, but nothing beats seeing things in person. A campus visit tells you a lot. You can observe classrooms. You can talk to teachers. Moreover, you can watch how students interact. A good school usually feels right the moment you walk in. It is structured and welcoming. Trust what you see. Sometimes, your observations reveal more than a glossy brochure.</span></span></p>
